# Task Management

All tasks are managed centrally in the **haderach-tasks** repo at `../haderach-tasks/tasks/`. This app repo does not have its own tasks directory.

## Creating a task from this repo

Write the task file to the appropriate `../haderach-tasks/tasks/` subdirectory (`features/`, `improvements/`, `chores/`, `docs/`) with `group: agent` and `phase: agent` in the frontmatter. Follow the conventions defined in `haderach-tasks/.cursor/rules/todo-conventions.mdc`.

Use plain integer IDs with no leading zeros (e.g., `"7"` not `"007"`). Read `../haderach-tasks/tasks/NEXT_ID` to get the next available ID, then increment the value in that file after creating the task.

If the task is ambiguous about which app it belongs to (e.g., cross-cutting infra work), prompt the user to specify the `group` value (`card`, `stocks`, `home`, `vendors`, `admin`, `agent`, or `platform`).

## Filing a bug from this repo

Write the bug file to `../haderach-tasks/tasks/bugs/` with `group: agent` and `phase: agent`. Follow the format in `haderach-tasks/.cursor/rules/bug-conventions.mdc`. Bugs use the same ID space as tasks.

## Reading tasks

When the user references a task by number (e.g., "task 29"), look it up in `../haderach-tasks/tasks/` by matching the `id` field or filename prefix (e.g., `29-*.md`). All tasks across all apps live there — the referenced task may belong to any group, not just `agent`.

To see tasks for this app, read files in `../haderach-tasks/tasks/` where the `group` frontmatter field is `agent`. Only read tasks where `status` is `pending` or `in-progress` unless specifically asked about others.
